[] — Array subscript / indexing operator.

() — Function call, grouping, cast, or expression precedence.

{} — Block delimiter, compound statement, or initializer list (C++/C99).

. — Direct member access (structure/class/union).

-> — Indirect member access (via pointer).

++ — Increment (prefix or postfix).

-- — Decrement (prefix or postfix).

& — Address‑of, bitwise AND, or reference declarator (C++).

* — Indirection (dereference) or multiplication.

+ — Addition or unary plus.

- — Subtraction or unary minus.

~ — Bitwise NOT (one’s complement).

! — Logical NOT.

/ — Division.

% — Modulo (remainder) operator.

<< — Bitwise left shift (or stream insertion in C++).

>> — Bitwise right shift (or stream extraction in C++).

< — Less‑than comparison.

> — Greater‑than comparison.

<= — Less‑than or equal to.

>= — Greater‑than or equal to.

== — Equality comparison.

!= — Inequality comparison.

^ — Bitwise XOR.

| — Bitwise OR.

&& — Logical AND (short‑circuit).

|| — Logical OR (short‑circuit).

? — Ternary conditional operator (start, paired with :).

: — Colon: labels, ternary ? :, bit‑fields, or inheritance (C++).

:: — Scope resolution operator (C++ – namespace/class/global).

; — Statement terminator.

... — Ellipsis (variadic arguments, or C++ fold expressions).

= — Simple assignment.

*= — Multiply‑and‑assign.

/= — Divide‑and‑assign.

%= — Modulo‑and‑assign.

+= — Add‑and‑assign.

-= — Subtract‑and‑assign.

<<= — Left‑shift‑and‑assign.

>>= — Right‑shift‑and‑assign.

&= — Bitwise‑AND‑and‑assign.

^= — Bitwise‑XOR‑and‑assign.

|= — Bitwise‑OR‑and‑assign.

, — Comma operator (evaluate left, discard, return right) or separator.

# — Preprocessor stringification (turn macro argument into a string literal).

## — Preprocessor token concatenation (join two tokens).

Digraphs (alternative tokens for readability on old keyboards):

<: — Digraph for [ (left bracket).

:> — Digraph for ] (right bracket).

<% — Digraph for { (left brace).

%> — Digraph for } (right brace).

%: — Digraph for # (preprocessor start).

%:%: — Digraph for ## (token concatenation).
